//! Wave F.1 follow-on (2026-05-27): `SpellCategoryDB` name lookup.
//!
//! Ports `ACE.Entity.Enum.SpellCategory` (730 entries) so plugins can
//! resolve `spell.category` u32 → human-readable name (e.g.
//! `StrengthRaising` for category 1). Useful for:
//!
//! * Tooltip stacking-conflict hints: "Strength X+5" can't stack with
//!   "Strength X+8" because both share `SpellCategory::StrengthRaising`.
//! * Spellbook category headers grouping spells by category instead of
//!   raw u32.
//! * Debug overlays showing what spell category a buff occupies.
//!
//! # Provenance
//!
//! The enum body is a verbatim port of
//! `external/ACE/Source/ACE.Entity/Enum/SpellCategory.cs` (734 lines,
//! 730 entries 0..733 with gaps at 622 + 700..703). Note Chorizite's
//! `Chorizite.Common/Enums/SpellCategory.cs` is a near-mirror but
//! types `SpellCategory` as `ushort` while ACE uses `uint` — the wire
//! ships these in a u16 / u32 depending on context, but the value
//! space is always sub-u16 in retail data, so the choice doesn't
//! affect lookup correctness.
//!
//! # Why ACE over the C++ `SpellCategoryDB`
//!
//! `external/chorizite/ACBindings/Generated/Game/Spells/SpellCategoryDB.cs`
//! is just a vtable scaffold with no enum-name data ("Functions as a
//! type marker within the spell subsystem"). The actual name table
//! lives in the unstripped `acclient.exe` only as the enum
//! `SpellCategory_*` symbols, not as runtime data. ACE's enum is the
//! authoritative *value → name* map.

/// Returns the human-readable name for a `SpellCategory` u32 value, or
/// `None` if no such category exists. O(log N) — implemented as a
/// binary search over a sorted const array.
///
/// ```ignore
/// use holtburger_protocol::messages::magic::spell_category_db::name;
/// assert_eq!(name(1), Some("StrengthRaising"));
/// assert_eq!(name(733), Some("GauntletCriticalDamageReductionRatingRaising"));
/// assert_eq!(name(701), None); // gap in enum
/// ```
pub fn name(category: u32) -> Option<&'static str> {
    SPELL_CATEGORY_NAMES
        .binary_search_by_key(&category, |(k, _)| *k)
        .ok()
        .map(|idx| SPELL_CATEGORY_NAMES[idx].1)
}

/// Returns the total number of named categories. Useful for tests.
pub fn count() -> usize {
    SPELL_CATEGORY_NAMES.len()
}

